      "output": "I'll start by invoking the ticket-writer skill.\nVerified the core claim by running the suite — the existing test is already red. Now drafting.\nBoth artifacts written. Summary:\n\n**Ticket:** *eh gateway validation: a blank plan provider key must suppress the ambient env fallback* — the single deferred `codex` finding from PR #49.\n\n**What discovery changed about the framing.** The review finding claimed a live credential-mismatch bug. It isn't reachable in production today: `resolveApiKey` is env-first (`src/keys.ts:246-251`), so ambient and the plan's `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` coincide whenever ambient is set, and reaching a diverging pair needs a hand-written config nothing in the repo suggests. Rather than overclaim, I anchored the ticket on a failure I **ran and confirmed** on the current checkout:\n\n```\n$ ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=[REDACTED] bun test src/gateway-routing.test.ts\nExpected: \"Bearer qa-auth-token\" / Received: \"Bearer ambient-leaked-key\"   17 pass, 1 fail\n```\n\nSo the fail-first proof is an *existing* test at `src/gateway-routing.test.ts:419` — zero new scaffolding, red before, green after. PR #49's contribution to that file was 6 lines of `delete process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` sanitization, which hides the precedence bug rather than fixing it; the ticket requires removing it if present on the implementer's base.\n\n**Three ACs:** (1) the precedence invariant *with* its complement — the ambient rung must still fire when `plan.env` doesn't own the key, since `planCodex`/`planPi`/`planOpencode` (`src/harnesses.ts:174`, `:278`, `:340`) depend on it and **no test covers that path**, so a wrong fix goes green; (2) the fail-first test with a deliberately-set ambient key; (3) one DESIGN.md paragraph recording the `resolveApiKey` env-first coupling, which is what keeps the latent divergence latent.\n\n**Kept whole** — one bounded behavior, one verification story, three files in one subsystem, no in-flight PR touches `src/gateway-routing.ts`. Independently dispatchable (the red test is on `main`). Out-of-scope calls out the two tempting creeps discovery flagged: an injected-`env` refactor (`src/pricing.ts:406` pattern) and \"aligning\" the `harnesses.ts` ambient checks.\n\nDelegability `low/medium` — design freedom low and verification high license a weak tier; `silent_failure_cost: medium` reflects the uncovered absent-key regression path, which the invariant's complement is written to constrain.\n\nNothing filed to Linear and no validation subagent run, per the pipeline contract.\n\nSTATUS:success\n",
